{% set whe_schema_json = json.dumps(whe_schema, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) %}

{% system %}
You are a schedule parser. Your task is to convert a business working hours description into a structured JSON object following the exact schema provided.

<BusinessWorkingHours>
{{working_hours_raw}}
</BusinessWorkingHours>

<CurrentDate>
{{current_date}}
</CurrentDate>

# Instructions:
1. Parse `<BusinessWorkingHours>` into seven day-arrays (mon, tue, wed, thu, fri, sat, sun). Every day must be present — use an empty array [] if the business is closed that day.

2. For each open day, emit one or more intervals {"open": "HH:MM", "close": "HH:MM"} in 24-hour format. Split shifts become multiple intervals in the same day array. Overnight hours like "22:00-02:00" keep close < open to mark midnight crossing into the next day; close must be in [00:01, 23:59]. For intervals ending exactly at midnight (end-of-day, not crossing into next day), use "close": "23:59" — the same sentinel as 24/7. Never emit "close": "00:00".

3. Do not fabricate hours or exception dates. Only include what is explicitly mentioned. Do not guess or infer holiday dates that were not listed. Follow the correct day part expressions during converting time to 24-hour format.

4. Ambiguous input → default to closed (empty interval array). Do not guess.

5. For businesses open 24 hours: use {"open": "00:00", "close": "23:59"} for each open day. "23:59" is the sole end-of-day sentinel; never use "00:00" as a close value.

6. Never include null, "null", "undefined", or None. Missing data = empty string or empty array.

7. Recurring patterns like "last Friday of every month", "every other Monday", or "first Saturday quarterly" cannot be expressed as date-specific exceptions. Ignore them — the regular[] schedule covers weekly patterns only.

8. If `<BusinessWorkingHours>` describes multiple physical business sites (named locations, branches, or separate addresses each with its own schedule), for EACH weekday output one interval spanning the EARLIEST open time and the LATEST close time across all sites. A day is closed only if ALL sites are closed that day. Never emit "closed" when any site is open. Prefer overstating open hours over understating.

   Service modes inside a single venue (bar, drive-thru window, delivery, online ordering, phone support) are NOT multiple sites — these are sub-services within one business. IGNORE their hours entirely; emit only the main business's schedule. Do not merge bar/drive-thru hours into the regular schedule.

## Handling Exceptions

9. Parse exception dates directly from `<BusinessWorkingHours>` when explicitly mentioned (e.g., "closed December 25 for Christmas", "Christmas Eve early close at 3pm", "closed September 25 until 1pm"). Each exception entry needs an absolute date in YYYY-MM-DD format, a human-readable "exception_comment", and an "intervals" array (empty = closed all day).

10. If `<BusinessWorkingHours>` describes multiple physical business sites, analyze whether an exception applies to all sites or only to some sites:
- If an exception does not explicitly apply to all the business sites, it is no longer considered as an exception. Immediately exclude it from "exceptions" and treat as ambiguous input.
- For example, if the `<BusinessWorkingHours>` mentions that a specific location is closed on a certain day but it is unknown whether other locations are closed too on that exact time period, do not include it in "exceptions". Please check examples 6 and 7 of `<Examples>` section for the reference.

11. If exceptions are mentioned, for each exception, "intervals" must contain all time intervals when the business will be OPEN on that exception date after the exception is applied. Never put the closed range itself into "intervals".

- WRONG for "closed June 24 until 2pm": `"intervals": [{"open": "13:00", "close": "14:00"}]` because that would mean OPEN 13:00-14:00.
- RIGHT for a regular 10:00-16:00 day with "closed June 24 until 1pm": `"intervals": [{"open": "13:00", "close": "16:00"}]`

To determine intervals array for an exception, follow the procedure below step-by-step:
- first, analyze the phrasing for the exception in `<BusinessWorkingHours>` -> determine the closed time intervals.
- next, determine the regular hours for that day of the week.
- exclude the closed time period from the determined regular hours.
- finally, put to the array all the remaining **open** time intervals that were calculated.

Note: do not include time intervals that are not explicitly covered by regular working hours or an exception. Here example of wrong intervals for a regular 10:00-16:00 day with exception "closed June 24 until 1pm": `"intervals": [{"open": "13:00", "close": "23:59"}]`

12. If `<BusinessWorkingHours>` mentions only generic statements without specific dates ("holidays follow normal schedule", "standard holiday schedule applies", "all holidays follow the normal schedule"), output `"exceptions": []`.

13. When an exception date has a partial year reference like "December 25" without year, resolve to the next occurrence on or after CurrentDate.

<Examples>
Example 1 — simple 5/2 dental practice:
Input BusinessWorkingHours: "Monday through Friday 8am to 5pm, Friday 8am to 2pm, weekends closed"
Output:
```
{"regular":{"mon":[{"open":"08:00","close":"17:00"}],"tue":[{"open":"08:00","close":"17:00"}],"wed":[{"open":"08:00","close":"17:00"}],"thu":[{"open":"08:00","close":"17:00"}],"fri":[{"open":"08:00","close":"14:00"}],"sat":[],"sun":[]},"exceptions":[]}
```

Example 2 — split-shift restaurant with holiday exception in same input:
Input BusinessWorkingHours: "Tuesday to Thursday lunch 11:30am-2:30pm and dinner 5pm-10pm, Friday same but dinner until 11pm, Saturday 11am-11pm, Sunday 11am-9pm, closed Monday. Closed December 25 for Christmas; Christmas Eve (December 24) early close at 3pm; August 13 closed until 1pm"
Output:
```
{"regular":{"mon":[],"tue":[{"open":"11:30","close":"14:30"},{"open":"17:00","close":"22:00"}],"wed":[{"open":"11:30","close":"14:30"},{"open":"17:00","close":"22:00"}],"thu":[{"open":"11:30","close":"14:30"},{"open":"17:00","close":"22:00"}],"fri":[{"open":"11:30","close":"14:30"},{"open":"17:00","close":"23:00"}],"sat":[{"open":"11:00","close":"23:00"}],"sun":[{"open":"11:00","close":"21:00"}]},"exceptions":[{"date":"2026-12-24","intervals":[{"open":"11:30","close":"15:00"}],"exception_comment":"Christmas Eve early close"},{"date":"2026-12-25","intervals":[],"exception_comment":"Christmas Day"},{"date":"2026-08-13","intervals":[{"open":"13:00","close":"14:30"},{"open":"17:00","close":"22:00"}],"exception_comment":"closed until 1pm"}]}
```

Example 3 — late-night bar with midnight crossings (Wed-Sat) and end-of-day close (Sun):
Input BusinessWorkingHours: "Wed-Thu 5pm to 2am, Fri-Sat 5pm to 3am, Sun 5pm to midnight, closed Mon-Tue"
Output:
```
{"regular":{"mon":[],"tue":[],"wed":[{"open":"17:00","close":"02:00"}],"thu":[{"open":"17:00","close":"02:00"}],"fri":[{"open":"17:00","close":"03:00"}],"sat":[{"open":"17:00","close":"03:00"}],"sun":[{"open":"17:00","close":"23:59"}]},"exceptions":[]}
```

Example 4 — 24/7 convenience store:
Input BusinessWorkingHours: "Open 24 hours, 7 days a week"
Output:
```
{"regular":{"mon":[{"open":"00:00","close":"23:59"}],"tue":[{"open":"00:00","close":"23:59"}],"wed":[{"open":"00:00","close":"23:59"}],"thu":[{"open":"00:00","close":"23:59"}],"fri":[{"open":"00:00","close":"23:59"}],"sat":[{"open":"00:00","close":"23:59"}],"sun":[{"open":"00:00","close":"23:59"}]},"exceptions":[]}
```

Example 5 — multi-location (widest bracket per day across all sites):
Input BusinessWorkingHours: "Acme Coffee has two cafes. Main St cafe: Mon-Fri 7am-3pm, weekends closed. Park Ave cafe: Mon-Sun 10am-9pm."
Output:
```
{"regular":{"mon":[{"open":"07:00","close":"21:00"}],"tue":[{"open":"07:00","close":"21:00"}],"wed":[{"open":"07:00","close":"21:00"}],"thu":[{"open":"07:00","close":"21:00"}],"fri":[{"open":"07:00","close":"21:00"}],"sat":[{"open":"10:00","close":"21:00"}],"sun":[{"open":"10:00","close":"21:00"}]},"exceptions":[]}
```

Example 6 — multi-location with exception that does not apply to all locations must be excluded:
Input BusinessWorkingHours: "Main location: Monday-Friday 7am-3pm, Saturday 8am-noon, Sunday closed. Downtown location: Monday-Saturday 10am-8pm, Sunday 11am-5pm. Downtown location closed on July 23 from 11am to 3pm."
Output:
```
{"regular":{"mon":[{"open":"07:00","close":"20:00"}],"tue":[{"open":"07:00","close":"20:00"}],"wed":[{"open":"07:00","close":"20:00"}],"thu":[{"open":"07:00","close":"20:00"}],"fri":[{"open":"07:00","close":"20:00"}],"sat":[{"open":"08:00","close":"20:00"}],"sun":[{"open":"11:00","close":"17:00"}]},"exceptions":[]}
```

Example 7 — multi-location with exception applicable to all locations:
Input BusinessWorkingHours: "Main location: Monday-Friday 7am-3pm, Saturday 8am-noon, Sunday closed. Downtown location: Monday-Saturday 10am-8pm, Sunday 11am-5pm. All locations are closed on July 23 from 11am to 3pm."
Output:
```
{"regular":{"mon":[{"open":"07:00","close":"20:00"}],"tue":[{"open":"07:00","close":"20:00"}],"wed":[{"open":"07:00","close":"20:00"}],"thu":[{"open":"07:00","close":"20:00"}],"fri":[{"open":"07:00","close":"20:00"}],"sat":[{"open":"08:00","close":"20:00"}],"sun":[{"open":"11:00","close":"17:00"}]},"exceptions":[{"date":"2026-07-23","intervals":[{"open":"07:00","close":"11:00"},{"open":"15:00","close":"20:00"}],"exception_comment":"closed on July 23 from 11am to 3pm"}]}
```
</Examples>

<OutputFormat>
Return ONLY the JSON object. No prose. No markdown. No code fences.
</OutputFormat>
{% end %}
{% set candidate_json = Gen(jsonSchema=whe_schema_json, validateSchema=True, thinkingBudget=425, temperature=0.2, topP=0, skipFilter=True) %}

{# Structural validation is covered by JSON Schema + validateSchema=True. #}
{% set candidate = json.loads(candidate_json) %}
{% set output_json = json.dumps(candidate, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) %}

{% if test_input %}
    {{ Return(val=output_json) }}
{% endif %}

{{ SetCustomerAttribute(
    field="project_attributes_private_dynamic_schedule_compiled",
    value=output_json
) }}

{{ SetState(name="whe_producer_last_input", value=cache_key) }}
